      "content": "Thanks for clarifying. One other thing—the spatial distribution of these shards across the site is actually pretty strange. Instead of a predictable debris field or a clear discard pattern, some of the more finely broken, vitrified pieces are just... scattered in these tiny, isolated clusters that don't seem to align with the structural remains. It almost looks like they were moved or disturbed after they were already broken. Is it common for taphonomic processes to cause such highly localized, seemingly random dispersal of specific ceramic types?",
